# Cloudflare sends these headers with every screen.
#
# Request 136: a private hospital tool, never indexed, never shown in search
# results, never kept in a search engine's copy.
#
# Request 155 (2026-11-08, security pass): the browser's own protections.
#   Content-Security-Policy: the page may only run its own code, and only
#     talk to itself and Supabase. A script slipped in from elsewhere does
#     not run, and no other site may show this app inside a frame
#     (frame-ancestors), so nobody can trick a nurse into clicking through
#     a disguised page. 'unsafe-inline' is needed by the Next.js build.
#   Strict-Transport-Security: always https, never plain http.
#   X-Content-Type-Options: a file is only ever treated as what it says.
#   Referrer-Policy: other sites never see which screen a link came from.
#   Permissions-Policy: no microphone or location; camera only for this app.
#   Cloudflare adds its own visitor counter script (Web Analytics) to the
#   page; the policy blocks it on purpose, because it would send screen
#   addresses (which carry patient numbers) out of the app. Harmless.
# Never: loosen these to make a new feature work without saying why here.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co; frame-src 'self' blob:; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
